ENFORCEMENT DECREE OF THE RURAL DEVELOPMENT ACT

Article 1 (Purpose)
The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Rural Development Act and matters necessary for its enforcement.

Article 2 (Scope of Rural Development Projects)
(1) "Duties concerning research and development prescribed by Presidential Decree" in subparagraph 2 (h) of Article 2 of the Rural Development Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") means the following duties: <Amended on July 9, 2019>
1. Research on adaptation to and impact assessment of climate change in agriculture, assessment of vulnerability to climate change, reduction of greenhouse gases, and energy savings;
2. Research on agricultural management, distribution and marketing of agricultural products, agricultural informatization, and farmers' welfare;
3. Research on technologies to resolve practical difficulties faced by farmers and rural communities and on safety management in agricultural work;
4. Research related to urban agriculture under subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Act on Development and Support of Urban Agriculture (hereinafter referred to in this Article as "urban agriculture");
5. Research on basic agricultural science and technology, primary agricultural products, and crops with export potential;
6. Other duties that the Administrator of the Rural Development Administration deems necessary and publicly notifies for research and development of new science and technology related to agriculture, farmers, and rural communities.
(2) "Duties concerning rural extension prescribed by Presidential Decree" in subparagraph 3 (g) of Article 2 of the Act means the following duties: <Amended on July 9, 2019; Jan. 29, 2020>
1. Support for revitalization of agriculture in areas outside rural communities, including urban agriculture;
2. Technical support for prevention of agricultural work accidents and daily living safety of older farmers;
3. Technical support for production of safe agricultural products, including environmentally friendly agriculture;
4. Support for agricultural development suited to regional characteristics;
5. Support for resolving practical difficulties faced by farmers and rural communities;
6. Establishment of and support for a scientific farming technology foundation to disseminate advanced technologies;
7. Other duties that the Administrator of the Rural Development Administration deems necessary and publicly notifies for dissemination of new research and development outcomes and management innovation of agricultural business entities.
(3) "Duties concerning education and training prescribed by Presidential Decree" in subparagraph 4 (d) of Article 2 of the Act means the following duties: <Amended on July 9, 2019>
1. Education and training for persons intending to engage in agriculture, including new farmers;
2. Agriculture-related education and training for persons in cities and other areas outside rural communities;
3. Education and training on repair, maintenance, and safe use of agricultural machinery;
4. Other duties that the Administrator of the Rural Development Administration deems necessary and publicly notifies to develop the capacities of public officials, farmers, etc. engaged in new rural development projects.
(4) "Duties concerning international cooperation prescribed by Presidential Decree" in subparagraph 5 (c) of Article 2 of the Act means the following duties:
1. Implementation of international cooperation projects concerning international norms related to agricultural technology;
2. Duties concerning international conferences in the field of agricultural technology;
3. Other duties prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs.

Article 3 (Formulation of Master Plans for Rural Development Projects, etc.)
(1) Before the beginning of the relevant business year, the Administrator of the Rural Development Administration shall formulate a master plan for rural development projects under Article 5 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "master plan") and an annual implementation plan (hereinafter referred to as an "implementation plan") following deliberation by the Rural Development Project Deliberation Committee under Article 6 (1) of the Act. In such cases, where necessary, the Administrator may request the heads of relevant central administrative agencies and local governments to provide data on the current state and forecasts of technologies in their respective fields, etc.
(2) The portions of master plans and implementation plans concerning research and development projects shall, after deliberation by the Rural Development Project Deliberation Committee under Article 6 (1) of the Act, undergo deliberation by the National Science and Technology Advisory Council under the National Science and Technology Advisory Council Act. <Added on Jan. 29, 2020>
(3) An implementation plan shall include the following: <Amended on Jan. 29, 2020>
1. Direction for promoting rural development projects;
2. Detailed plans and investment plans for each field of rural development projects;
3. Other matters that the Administrator of the Rural Development Administration deems necessary for promoting rural development projects.
(4) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) through (3), matters necessary for formulation and amendment of master plans and implementation plans, etc. shall be prescribed by the Administrator of the Rural Development Administration. <Amended on Jan. 29, 2020>

Article 4 (Composition and Operation of the Rural Development Project Deliberation Committee)
(1) The Rural Development Project Deliberation Committee under Article 6 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to in this Article as the "Committee") shall consist of no more than 20 members, including one chairperson.
(2) The Deputy Administrator of the Rural Development Administration shall serve as chairperson of the Committee (hereinafter referred to in this Article as the "chairperson"), and members shall be the following persons: <Amended on Sept. 23, 2015; Dec. 23, 2025>
1. Ex officio members: Four persons holding positions designated by the Administrator of the Rural Development Administration from among officials of that Administration belonging to the Senior Civil Service;
2. Private-sector members: Persons with extensive expertise and experience in agriculture, rural communities, and rural development projects, commissioned by the Administrator of the Rural Development Administration with consideration for gender. In such cases, persons recommended by an association established under Article 182 (1) 1 or 3 of the Local Autonomy Act shall be included.
(3) The term of office of private-sector members under paragraph (2) 2 shall be two years, and they may be reappointed consecutively only once.
(4) The chairperson shall represent the Committee and exercise overall control over its affairs.
(5) Where the chairperson is unable to perform duties for unavoidable reasons, a member designated in advance by the chairperson shall act on the chairperson's behalf.
(6) The chairperson shall convene and preside over Committee meetings.
(7) A majority of the incumbent members shall constitute a quorum for Committee meetings, and resolutions shall require the affirmative vote of a majority of the members present.
(8) The Committee shall have one secretary to handle its administrative affairs, designated by the Administrator of the Rural Development Administration from among officials of that Administration.
(9) Allowances and travel expenses may be paid within budgetary limits to members, experts, etc. attending the Committee; provided, this shall not apply where a member who is a public official or a relevant public official attends the Committee in direct connection with official duties.
(10) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) through (9), matters necessary for the operation of the Committee shall be determined by the chairperson following a resolution of the Committee.

Article 4-2 (Dismissal of Members)
The Administrator of the Rural Development Administration may dismiss a member under Article 4 (2) 2 in any of the following cases:
1. Where the member becomes unable to perform duties due to a mental or physical disability;
2. Where the member has committed misconduct related to duties;
3. Where the member is deemed unsuitable due to neglect of duties, impairment of dignity, or other reasons;
4. Where the member states that it is difficult to perform the duties.

Article 5 (Selection of Research Tasks by Field for Joint Research Projects, etc.)
(1) To conduct joint research projects under Article 7 (1) of the Act, the Administrator of the Rural Development Administration shall formulate a joint research project plan each year as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs. In such cases, the joint research project plan shall include the contents of joint research projects or joint research tasks and other matters prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs.
(2) When selecting research and development tasks by field and the research and development institutions to perform them under Article 7 (2) of the Act, the Administrator of the Rural Development Administration shall make the selection in accordance with Article 9 (4) of the National Research and Development Innovation Act. <Amended on Mar. 26, 2024>

Article 6 (Agreements for Joint Research Projects, etc.)
(1) Conclusion, amendment, cancellation, etc. of agreements under Article 7 (2) of the Act shall be governed by Article 11 of the National Research and Development Innovation Act. <Amended on Mar. 26, 2024>
(2) Reporting by the head of a research and development institution that has concluded an agreement under Article 7 (2) of the Act on the use of research and development expenses, and settlement of those expenses, shall be governed by Articles 25 and 26 of the Enforcement Decree of the National Research and Development Innovation Act. <Amended on Mar. 26, 2024>
(3) Matters necessary concerning payment methods, management, etc. of contributions made under Article 7 (3) of the Act shall be prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs.

Article 7 (Deliberation and Coordination of Research and Development Projects)
(1) The Administrator of the Rural Development Administration shall formulate basic guidelines for deliberation and coordination of the duties specified in the subparagraphs of Article 10 of the Act and perform deliberation and coordination duties on the basis of those guidelines.
(2) Upon formulating basic guidelines under paragraph (1), the Administrator of the Rural Development Administration shall notify the heads of its affiliated institutions and the heads of local rural development institutions under Article 3 of the Act (meaning local rural development organizations under Article 16 of the Regulations on Administrative Organizations and Personnel Standards of Local Governments; hereinafter referred to as "local rural development institutions").

Article 8 (Transfer of Research and Development Outcomes, etc.)
(1) Payment of a portion of royalties or proceeds under the main clause of Article 13 (1) of the Act shall be governed by Article 38 or 39 of the Enforcement Decree of the National Research and Development Innovation Act. <Amended on Mar. 26, 2024>
(2) The Administrator of the Rural Development Administration may reduce or exempt all or part of the payments for use, etc. of research and development outcomes (hereinafter referred to in this paragraph as "outcomes") under the proviso of Article 13 (1) of the Act in the following cases: <Amended on Sept. 23, 2015; Mar. 26, 2024>
1. Where outcomes need to be disseminated rapidly nationwide to increase farmers' income;
2. Where dissemination of outcomes is necessary for development of domestic industries, including export promotion or import substitution;
3. Where outcomes need to be disseminated nationwide to conserve the agricultural environment;
4. Where dissemination of outcomes is necessary to implement government policies, including support for and fostering of small and medium enterprises;
5. Where the research and development institution owning the outcomes falls under either of the following:
(a) A producer organization under subparagraph 4 of Article 3 of the Framework Act on Agriculture, Rural Community and Food Industry;
(b) An agricultural partnership corporation under Article 16 of the Act on Fostering and Supporting Agricultural and Fisheries Business Entities or an agricultural company corporation under Article 19 of that Act;
6. Where the Administrator of the Rural Development Administration otherwise deems dissemination of outcomes particularly necessary to strengthen agricultural competitiveness.

Article 9 (Use of Service Inventions with Pending Patent Applications)
Where the Administrator of the Rural Development Administration intends to have a technology researched and developed by an affiliated public official in connection with official duties (hereinafter referred to as a "service invention"), for which a patent application is pending (including a utility model; hereinafter the same shall apply), commercialized under Article 13 (3) of the Act, the Administrator shall conclude a contract for its use with the person intending to commercialize it, as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs, and collect royalties; provided, in cases falling under Article 8 (2) 1 through 4 or 6, all or part of the royalties may be reduced or exempted.

Article 10 (Processing of Personally Identifiable Information)
The Administrator of the Rural Development Administration may process materials containing resident registration numbers under subparagraph 1 of Article 19 of the Enforcement Decree of the Personal Information Protection Act where unavoidable to perform affairs concerning conclusion of contracts under Article 9 (1) in connection with the use of service inventions with pending patent applications under Article 13 (3) of the Act. <Amended on Sept. 23, 2015; Mar. 26, 2024>

Article 11 (Requirements for Pilot Projects)
A pilot project under Article 16 of the Act shall meet any of the following requirements:
1. Early dissemination of research and development outcomes to agricultural sites shall be necessary;
2. Urgent implementation for the development of agriculture and rural communities shall be necessary;
3. It shall concern an agricultural technology that the Administrator of the Rural Development Administration considers likely to produce substantial effects as a pilot project, from among agricultural technologies proposed by local rural development institutions, universities, farmers, etc.

Article 12 Deleted. <Sept. 23, 2015>

Article 13 (Cooperation with Other Education and Training Institutions)
Where a public organization conducts education and training projects among rural development projects under Article 27 of the Act, it shall cooperate with the Rural Development Administration and local rural development institutions on the following:
1. Formulation and implementation of education and training plans;
2. Compilation of education and training materials;
3. Joint use of education and training facilities, equipment, and practical training plots;
4. Provision of education and training instructors;
5. Follow-up management of persons who have completed education and training;
6. Financial support necessary to conduct education and training.

Article 14 (Utilization of Retired Research and Extension Officials)
(1) A system for utilizing retired research and extension officials under Article 31 (3) and (4) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "utilization system") shall include the following:
1. Fields and duties for utilization;
2. Number and qualifications of persons to be utilized;
3. Recruitment methods and procedures;
4. Service and management of recruited personnel;
5. Other matters that the Administrator of the Rural Development Administration deems necessary for efficient utilization of retired research and extension officials.
(2) Where the Administrator of the Rural Development Administration has established or amended the utilization system, the Administrator shall publicly announce it through the Official Gazette, the website of the Rural Development Administration, or other means.
(3) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) and (2), details necessary for establishment and operation of the utilization system shall be prescribed by the Administrator of the Rural Development Administration.

Article 15 Deleted. <Mar. 26, 2024>

Article 16 Deleted. <Mar. 26, 2024>

Article 17 Deleted. <Mar. 26, 2024>

Article 18 (Scope of Business of the Korea Agriculture Technology Promotion Agency)
"Business prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 33 (3) 9 of the Act means the following business: <Amended on Feb. 22, 2022>
1. Testing, analysis, and evaluation related to products, technologies, etc. for practical application of research and development outcomes;
2. Multiplication and dissemination of seeds and seedlings developed by the State or local governments for urgent dissemination.

Article 19 (Contributions and Support to the Korea Agriculture Technology Promotion Agency)
A person intending to contribute or provide support for expenses or costs under Article 34 (1) or (3) of the Act may conclude an agreement with the Korea Agriculture Technology Promotion Agency under Article 33 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Agency") on the amount, timing, methods, etc. of the contribution or support. <Amended on Feb. 22, 2022>

Article 20 (Institutions Contributing or Providing Support for Expenses)
(1) "Institutions prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 34 (1) 2 of the Act means the following institutions:
1. The Korea Racing Authority under the Korea Racing Authority Act;
2. The Korea Food Research Institute under the Act on the Establishment, Operation and Fostering of Government-Funded Science and Technology Research Institutes.
(2) "Persons prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 34 (1) 5 of the Act means the following persons: <Amended on Dec. 22, 2015>
1. Producer organizations under subparagraph 4 of Article 3 of the Framework Act on Agriculture, Rural Community and Food Industry;
2. Agricultural partnership corporations under Article 16 of the Act on Fostering and Supporting Agricultural and Fisheries Business Entities and agricultural company corporations under Article 19 of that Act;
3. Companies under the Commercial Act related to agriculture or food.

Article 21 (Revenue-Generating Business of the Agency)
(1) Where the Agency intends to conduct revenue-generating business under Article 34 (2) of the Act, it shall submit a revenue-generating business plan to the Administrator of the Rural Development Administration for approval. The same shall apply where an approved revenue-generating business plan is amended. <Amended on Feb. 22, 2022>
(2) Within three months after the end of the relevant business year, the Agency shall submit to the Administrator of the Rural Development Administration a performance report and statement of accounts for the revenue-generating business approved under paragraph (1). <Amended on Feb. 22, 2022>

Article 22 (Transfer of State and Public Property without Compensation, etc.)
(1) The period of permission to use or lease State or public property and goods under Article 34 (4) of the Act shall not exceed five years, and the permission to use or lease contract may be renewed for a period not exceeding five years. <Amended on Sept. 23, 2015>
(2) A person intending to renew permission to use or a lease contract under paragraph (1) shall apply for renewal to the managing authority of the relevant State or public property and goods no later than one month before the permission or lease period expires. <Amended on Sept. 23, 2015>
(3) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) and (2), the details, conditions, and procedures for transfer, lease, and permission for use and profit-making with respect to State or public property and goods under Article 34 of the Act shall be determined by contract between the managing authority of the relevant property or goods and the Agency. <Added on Sept. 23, 2015; Amended on Feb. 22, 2022>

Article 23 (Delegation and Entrustment of Authority, etc.)
(1) Pursuant to Article 36 (1) of the Act, the Administrator of the Rural Development Administration shall delegate to the heads of affiliated institutions authority concerning conclusion of contracts for use of service inventions with pending patent applications under Article 9 (1) of this Decree (limited to matters concerning selection of contracting parties and determination, reduction, and exemption of royalties). <Amended on Mar. 26, 2024>
(2) Pursuant to the former part of Article 36 (2) of the Act, the Administrator of the Rural Development Administration shall entrust to the Agency duties concerning conclusion of contracts for use of service inventions with pending patent applications under Article 9 (1) of this Decree (excluding matters concerning selection of contracting parties and determination, reduction, and exemption of royalties) and collection of the resulting royalties. <Amended on Feb. 22, 2022>
(3) The Administrator of the Rural Development Administration shall pay the Agency an amount equivalent to 175 per 1,000 of the royalties collected by the Agency under paragraph (2). <Amended on Feb. 22, 2022>
(4) Pursuant to the former part of Article 36 (2) of the Act, the Administrator of the Rural Development Administration may entrust education and training projects under Article 19 of the Act to institutions or organizations falling under the following subparagraphs that meet the standards for facilities, personnel, etc. prescribed by the Administrator: <Added on Sept. 23, 2015>
1. Institutions related to education and training;
2. Organizations related to farmers or young people for promoting the sustainable development of agriculture and rural communities.
(5) Where the Administrator of the Rural Development Administration entrusts duties under paragraph (4), the Administrator shall publicly notify the entrusted institution. <Added on Sept. 23, 2015>
(6) Where the Administrator of the Rural Development Administration entrusts education and training projects under paragraph (4), the Administrator may provide support for expenses necessary for conducting education and improving facilities. <Added on Sept. 23, 2015>

ADDENDA <Presidential Decree No. 25179, Feb. 13, 2014>

Article 1 (Enforcement Date)
This Decree shall enter into force on February 14, 2014.

Article 2 (Transitional Measures concerning Reports on Execution of Contributions)
Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 6 (2), submission of reports on execution of contributions by the head of a lead institution for joint research or the principal investigator of a joint research and development project that has received contributions under an agreement pursuant to the former Article 6 (1) as at the time this Decree enters into force shall be governed by the former provisions.

Article 3 (Amendments to Other Statutes and Regulations)
(1) The Enforcement Decree of the Act on Promotion of Science and Technology for Food, Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries shall be amended as follows:
In Article 6 (2) 1 (e), "Article 14-2 of the Rural Development Act" shall be replaced by "Article 33 of the Rural Development Act."
(2) The Enforcement Decree of the Pesticide Control Act shall be amended as follows:
In the main sentence of Article 22 (3), "Article 14-2 of the Rural Development Act" shall be replaced by "Article 33 of the Rural Development Act."
(3) The Enforcement Decree of the Agricultural Mechanization Promotion Act shall be amended as follows:
In the main sentence of Article 9 (2), "Article 14-2 (1) of the Rural Development Act" shall be replaced by "Article 33 of the Rural Development Act."
(4) The Regulations on the Agricultural Industry-Academia Cooperation Deliberation Council shall be amended as follows:
In Article 1, "experimental research projects, rural extension projects, and education and training projects under Article 2 of the Rural Development Act" shall be replaced by "rural development projects under subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Rural Development Act."
In subparagraph 1 of Article 6, "experimental research projects, rural extension projects, and education and training projects under Article 2 of the Rural Development Act" shall be replaced by "rural development projects under subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Rural Development Act."
(5) The Enforcement Decree of the Act on the Allocation and Trading of Greenhouse-Gas Emission Permits shall be amended as follows:
In Article 49 (2) 1, "Article 14-2 of the Rural Development Act" shall be replaced by "Article 33 of the Rural Development Act."

Article 4 (Relationship to Other Statutes and Regulations)
Where other statutes and regulations cite the former Enforcement Decree of the Rural Development Act or its provisions as at the time this Decree enters into force, and corresponding provisions exist in this Decree, they shall be deemed to cite this Decree or its corresponding provisions in place of the former provisions.

